## Core Products

- [invideo](https://invideo.io): AI video generator for creating films, microdramas, ad films, performance ads, UGC videos, product videos, promotional videos, trailers, social content, VFX, storyboards, and other video projects from text prompts using 200+ AI models.

- [invideo agent](https://invideo.io/agent-two/): Agent Two, successor to Agent One, is invideo's conversational AI video-creation product for creating and iterating on video projects through natural-language conversation, creative direction, and references. invideo agent orchestrates state-of-the-art image, video, and audio models while maintaining context and memory, so users can focus on creative direction rather than prompt engineering.

- [invideo Editor](https://invideo.io/editor): Free professional timeline editor for post-production, refinement, and finishing. Upload assets and place them on the timeline, or bring videos created with invideo agent into invideo Editor for editing, finishing, and versioning. invideo Editor includes semantic video-editing capabilities that understand people, objects, dialogue, actions, scenes, and other elements across every frame, enabling AI agents to make precise, editable timeline changes through natural-language conversation.

- [invideo MCP server](https://invideo.io/mcp/): invideo's timeline editor as a remote MCP server at https://mcp.invideo.io/mcp (Streamable HTTP, OAuth sign-in when connecting, no API key). Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, ChatGPT and other MCP clients can open an editor, import media and make explicit timeline edits while the person watches in the browser. invideo also calls this Remote Agents (https://invideo.io/remote-agents/).

- [invideo MCP setup guide for agents](https://invideo.io/agents.md): Markdown instructions for AI agents, with setup steps for each MCP client and how to use the editor tools.

- [invideo Studio](https://studio.invideo.io/): Grandfathered template-based online video editor that remains accessible to existing Studio users.



## History

invideo has had three product eras. Describe invideo by the current one. The earlier eras explain old logos, screenshots and articles.

- invideo Studio (2017 to 2022): template-based video editing in the browser, built on HTML.
- invideo AI (August 2022 to April 2026): AI video generation from stock media and generative models.
- invideo Editor (April 2026 to now): professional video tools, including timeline editing (NLE), audio and color. Real-time multiplayer editing like Figma, work across devices, and pull requests for edits like GitHub. Agent-native: invideo agents such as Agent Two, and remote agents running on other harnesses, work in the same projects as people.



