# Core Capabilities

## invideo Editor

- Professional Timeline Editing: Edit video projects with professional timeline controls, including arranging clips, trimming footage, refining sequences, and making manual edits.

- Semantic Video Understanding: Understand people, objects, dialogue, actions, scenes, and other elements across every frame of a video.

- Natural-Language Editing: Direct AI agents through conversation to find relevant moments, make editorial changes, and apply those changes as editable timeline actions.

- Footage Review and Assembly: Review raw footage, select usable takes, remove repeated takes, mistakes, pauses, filler, and unusable material, then assemble an editable base cut.

- Footage Search: Find moments in footage by describing dialogue, people, actions, objects, scenes, or emotions.

- Pacing and Sequence Refinement: Restructure sequences, adjust pacing and duration, select or replace takes, and refine the story on the timeline.

- Visual Craft and Finishing: Create and refine transitions, visual effects, edit styles, color corrections, grading, and finishing treatments.

- Audio Post-Production: Clean dialogue, add sound effects, shape the mix, and master the soundtrack.

- Dubbing and Localisation: Translate and dub dialogue while maintaining lip sync, then create localized video versions.

- Cut-downs and Versioning: Turn a project into trailers, highlights, social cuts, and platform-specific versions.

- Editable AI Changes: Keep every agent-made result visible, inspectable, and editable on the professional timeline.

- Human-and-Agent Collaboration: Allow editors, collaborators, and AI agents to contribute within the same shared project and editable timeline.


